# CrewSafety setup file for teammates
#
# HOW TO USE (3 steps)
#   1. Copy this file to a new file called  .env  in the repo root (same folder as README.md):
#        cp .env.teammates .env
#   2. Fill in the blanks below. Ask Andrew for the keys in a private message. Never paste them in a
#      group chat, a screenshot, a GitHub issue or a commit.
#   3. Start the website:   cd web && npm start      then open http://127.0.0.1:4173
#
# .env is git-ignored, so it will not be committed. Do not rename it to anything else.
# Everything is optional: with no keys the website still runs, and only the matching feature turns off.

# ── MUSE (Meta): journal reflections, photo descriptions, Camera Coach ──
# Without a key those buttons say "MUSE is not configured". Everything else works.
META_API_KEY=
META_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3

# ── ElevenLabs: spoken alert clips, phone calls, and the live voice check-in ──
# One key covers all three. Without it the voice agent checkbox stays off.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# The agent you talk to during the live "Are you OK?" check-in (safe to leave as is):
ELEVENLABS_CHECKIN_AGENT_ID=agent_7501m7f8gfk6e7taqqf0c27mwyxt
# Only needed for alert PHONE CALLS (you can skip these two):
ELEVENLABS_ALERT_AGENT_ID=
ELEVENLABS_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# ── Web Push notifications (skip unless you are testing push) ──
# Make your own pair with:  node web/scripts/generate-vapid.mjs
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# ── Quick fixes ──
# * Changed something here? Stop the server (Ctrl+C) and run  npm start  again.
# * Page looks old? In the browser, hard refresh (Cmd+Shift+R) so it drops the cached copy.
# * The iPhone app needs no .env. In the iOS Simulator, set the website address in its Settings to
#   http://127.0.0.1:4173 and turn on "Talk with the voice agent" to use the voice check-in.
#   (A real iPhone cannot reach npm start, which only listens on this computer.)
